meta {
  name: Delete DataSink
  type: http
  seq: 7
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/datasets/:dataSetId/datasinks/:id
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  ~confirmedRemovalIds:
}

params:path {
  dataSetId: {{dataSetId}}
  id: {{dataSinkId}}
}

tests {
  test("DataSink deleted", function() {
    const status = res.getStatus();
    // 204=deleted, 404=already gone from a previous run.
    expect(status === 204 || status === 404).to.be.true;
  });
}

docs {
  **Precondition:** `dataSetId` and `dataSinkId` are set. The DataSet is in `DRAFT`.

  A direct delete applies only to a DataSink that no Pipeline links. For a linked DataSink the backend answers `409` with type `urn:civitas:error:RESOURCE_IN_USE` and changes nothing: remove the DataSink from its Pipelines first (Pipeline `PUT`/`PATCH` without it in `dataSinkIds`, or the Pipeline delete).

  The delete makes the DataSink inactive. In the same transaction:

  - A DataSink that was never provisioned is deleted together with its Layers. A provisioned one is marked `PENDING_UNPROVISION`: its Layers are deleted, the record stays until the next release removes its storage, and it is no longer returned by the DataSink endpoints (`404`).
  - An API of the DataSet goes, together with its Layers, when no active DataSink of a kind that backs it remains: PostGIS for OWS, FROST for STA.

  **Confirmation:** When the delete removes a provisioned DataSink, a Layer or an API, the request must name each of them in `confirmedRemovalIds` (repeatable UUID query parameter). Get the ids from `datasets/get-removal-impact` with `deletedDataSinkIds`, or from the `impact` of a `409`. Without them the backend answers `409` with type `urn:civitas:error:REMOVAL_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED` and changes nothing. The DataSink of this collection is not provisioned and backs no Layer or API, so it goes without confirmation.

  **Expected Response:** 204 No Content. 409 `RESOURCE_IN_USE` if a Pipeline still links the DataSink. 409 `REMOVAL_CONFIRMATION_REQUIRED` with property `impact` (`dataSinks`, `layers`, `apis`, `requiresConfirmation`) if the confirmation is missing or incomplete.

  **Verification:** Issue `get-datasink-by-id` for the same `dataSinkId` and confirm 404.

  **System Impact:**

  | Layer | Effect |
  |---|---|
  | Backend | DataSink deleted or marked `PENDING_UNPROVISION`; its Layers deleted; APIs without an active backing DataSink deleted |
  | Config Adapter | the next release removes the storage of a `PENDING_UNPROVISION` DataSink |
  | External System | — |
}
